pr_comments:
@andypiper appreciate the response. I think it might be helpful if in Trunks & Tidbits you addressed how you prioritize contributions that appear "done" and what the bar is for getting a contribution included in upstream. Like, in this PR's case -- and the PRs that preceded it -- what is missing to make it "done"? Is it documentation? Is it unit tests? Do you disagree with the approach? I'm not seeing anything that stands out based on https://github.com/mastodon/mastodon/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md.

If the concern is the load it's going to put on the upstream team and that it might upset other "roadmap" items, what needs to be true such that, as contributors, we can minimize this to ship what appears to be a very simple PR? Again, if simple things like this can't get through over the course of years, why, as a potential future contributor, would I bother to attempt anything "big"?

Again, I appreciate the response, but just as you say you have to "prioritize our time", I would like to prioritize mine, too. As an admin of a middle-sized Mastodon instance, I'd like to spend the volunteer hours I put into running Hachyderm on the more important aspects, not the toil of remembering to hot patch a character limit increase or sync'ing a fork. How do we make this true?
